    "updated_at": "2026-11-09T19:03:44Z",
    "body": "**Judgement calls for the maintainer** (headless: app layer plus MCP, no GUI change; touched suites and clippy green; the GUI entry point is follow-up #511):\n1. **Recognised slots with round or open ends become Slot ops,** even though #510 (a typed Slot whose cutter reaches its round end is reported as a gouge, already on main) blocks posting them until it's fixed. The alternative was a Pocket over the floor, which posts today but leaves the open-end corners uncut; switching is one line in `recognize/op.rs`.\n2. **Top Z is the highest wall point next to the floor:** the op may cut a little air but never starts below material.\n3. **A recognised Slot's source is the stock, not the model,** so the end that runs out of the part isn't flagged.\n4. **Thresholds are tuning calls:** opposite-wall cosine below -0.9, slot length at least 2 widths, 3% area match, corners turning more than 60° count as sharp.\n5. **Not recognised yet:** through pockets and windows, floors that aren't level or tilted setups, curved slots and T-slots, and a stepped pocket as one feature (each level is listed separately).",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
